course: dictionary
lesson: 16143
title: Wilfulness: stubborn or on purpose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wilfulness means being set on doing what you want, even when you are told not to. «Tom's wilfulness meant he refused to put on his coat, even though it was snowing.» Tom would not listen, so wilfulness must mean stubbornness.
explain: In law and formal writing, wilfulness means doing something on purpose, when you know it is wrong. «The vandal caused wilful damage to the bus shelter.» The clue is damage: the word tells you the damage was not an accident.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Put stubbornness in place of wilfulness: «Tom's stubbornness meant he refused to put on his coat.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Wilfulness means being determined to do what you want, even when you are told not to.
fact: Wilfulness is another word for stubbornness.
fact: In law, wilfulness means doing something on purpose, knowing it is wrong.
fact: «Wilful damage» means damage done on purpose, not by accident.
fact: In US English the word is spelled willfulness, with one l.
exercise: «Tom's wilfulness meant he refused to put on his coat, even though it was snowing.» What does wilfulness mean here? | *Stubbornness, refusing to do what you are told | Kindness to animals | Being very cold | Speed in running
exercise: «The vandal caused wilful damage to the bus shelter.» What does wilful mean in this sentence? | Very slowly | *On purpose | By accident | In the rain
exercise: «Her wilfulness got her into trouble again.» What does this tell you about her? | She was lost and frightened | She was very tired and sleepy | She was happy to help everyone | *She insisted on doing it her own way, even after being told no
test: Which word is closest in meaning to wilfulness? | Kindness | Speed | Laughter | *Stubbornness
test: Which sentence uses wilfulness correctly? | The sun was bright and warm all day | She shared her toys happily with her friends | *He refused to leave the park, even when his mum asked him three times | The bread was fresh from the oven
exam: In a law case, what does wilfulness mean? | *Doing something on purpose, knowing it is wrong | Being strong and fit | Losing things by accident | Kind help given to a friend
